{"task_id": "HumanEval/44", "solution": "def change_base(x: int, base: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Change numerical base of input number x to base.\n    return string representation after the conversion.\n    base numbers are less than 10.\n    >>> change_base(8, 3)\n    '22'\n    >>> change_base(8, 2)\n    '1000'\n    >>> change_base(7, 2)\n    '111'\n    \"\"\"\n    def _validate_base(base: int) -> None:\n        \"\"\"\n        Validates if the provided base is an integer and less than 10.\n        Raises TypeError if base is not an int, ValueError if base is >= 10.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(base, int):\n            raise TypeError(\"Base must be an integer.\")\n        if base >= 10:\n            raise ValueError(\"Base must be less than 10.\")\n\n    _validate_base(base)\n\n    if x == 0:\n        return '0'\n\n    res_digits = []\n    current_x = x\n    while current_x > 0:\n        remainder = current_x % base\n        res_digits.append(str(remainder))\n        current_x //= base\n\n    # The digits are collected in reverse order, so reverse them before joining\n    return \"\".join(res_digits[::-1])"}
