{"task_id": "HumanEval/49", "solution": "def modp(n: int, p: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Return 2^n modulo p using exponentiation by squaring.\n    This ensures numeric stability and efficiency for large inputs.\n    \"\"\"\n    res = 1\n    base = 2\n\n    # Ensure base is within modulus for initial calculation.\n    base %= p\n\n    while n > 0:\n        # If n is odd, incorporate current base into result.\n        if n % 2 == 1:\n            res = (res * base) % p\n\n        # Square the base for the next iteration.\n        base = (base * base) % p\n\n        # Halve n.\n        n //= 2\n\n    return res"}
