{"task_id": "HumanEval/50", "solution": "def decode_shift(s: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Decodes an input string by reversing a 5-character Caesar cipher shift on lowercase English alphabet characters.\n    It handles alphabet wrapping for characters that would shift below 'a'.\n    \"\"\"\n    decoded_chars = []\n    for ch in s:\n        pos = ord(ch) - ord('a')\n        shifted_pos = pos - 5\n        wrapped_pos = shifted_pos % 26\n        decoded_ascii = wrapped_pos + ord('a')\n        decoded_char = chr(decoded_ascii)\n        decoded_chars.append(decoded_char)\n    return \"\".join(decoded_chars)"}
