{"task_id": "HumanEval/50", "solution": "def _shift_char(char: str, shift_amount: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Shifts an alphabetic character backward by a given amount, wrapping around.\n    Non-alphabetic characters are returned unchanged.\n    \"\"\"\n    if 'a' <= char <= 'z':\n        base = ord('a')\n        return chr((ord(char) - base - shift_amount + 26) % 26 + base)\n    elif 'A' <= char <= 'Z':\n        base = ord('A')\n        return chr((ord(char) - base - shift_amount + 26) % 26 + base)\n    else:\n        return char\ndef decode_shift(s: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Decodes a string by shifting alphabetic characters backward by 5 positions, wrapping around.\n    Non-alphabetic characters are left unchanged.\n    \"\"\"\n    decoded_chars = []\n    for char in s:\n        decoded_chars.append(_shift_char(char, 5))\n    return \"\".join(decoded_chars)"}
