{"task_id": "HumanEval/60", "solution": "def sum_to_n(n: int):\n    \"\"\"sum_to_n is a function that sums numbers from 1 to n.\n    >>> sum_to_n(30)\n    465\n    >>> sum_to_n(100)\n    5050\n    >>> sum_to_n(5)\n    15\n    >>> sum_to_n(10)\n    55\n    >>> sum_to_n(1)\n    1\n    \"\"\"\n    # This calculates the sum using the arithmetic series formula.\n    # The result is guaranteed to be an integer.\n    return n * (n + 1) // 2"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/59", "solution": "def largest_prime_factor(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the largest prime factor of n.\n    Assumes n is an integer greater than 1 and not a prime number.\n    \"\"\"\n    largest_factor = -1\n\n    # Divide by 2 until n is odd\n    while n % 2 == 0:\n        largest_factor = 2\n        n //= 2\n\n    # Check for odd factors from 3 up to sqrt(n)\n    i = 3\n    while i * i <= n:\n        while n % i == 0:\n            largest_factor = i\n            n //= i\n        i += 2  # Move to the next odd number\n\n    # If n is still greater than 1, it must be the largest prime factor\n    if n > 1:\n        largest_factor = n\n\n    return largest_factor"}
